  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 307 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nHigh clouds are streaming east across the northern Plains and \nUpper Midwest as a short wave trough begins to dig southeast \ninto ND. This trough will continue southeast today, swinging \nthrough MN and WI later this morning. This will bring a chance \nof showers across southern MN, but dry high pressure in place \nwill limit any amounts to a couple hundredths at best. Clearing \nskies will occur this afternoon. \n\nThe high will slide east to the Great Lakes tonight and warm \nair advection will begin across the Upper Midwest as a potent \ntrough advances into the northern Plains. Very strong moisture \nadvection will be brought on by a 55 kt LLJ Monday and pwats are\nexpected to increase to just short of 2 inches. Isentropic lift\nwill allow widespread showers to develop across the region, but\nthe trough will swing through quickly and limit the residence \ntime of the steadier activity. Scattered showers and \nthunderstorms may redevelop behind the main round as moisture \nadvection continues into early Monday evening and a moist warm \nnose around 800 mb allows elevated instability to increase. That\npotential will be short-lived as drier air begins to work in as\nthe evening wears on. A front will drape itself from northern \nWI to southeast MN and northwest IA Monday night. The LLJ will \nimpinge on the front allowing for a band of showers and\nthunderstorms to continue before sliding southeast Tuesday. The\nhighest QPF will be found in this corridor with 1-2 inches \nexpected.\n\nZonal flow will continue this week with mid level ridging \nremaining anchored in place across the southeast and \nstrengthening to 600 dam by Wednesday. A nearly stationary \nfront will be draped from the central Plains to mid Mississippi\nValley Tuesday and Wednesday, keeping any shower and \nthunderstorm chances well to the south. The front may work north\nlater in the week as the ridge builds over the southeast. PoPs\nincrease after Wednesday and remain in the forecast into Friday,\naccounting for low confidence with timing. \n\nSeasonably cool air will remain in place until further notice \nwith highs in the 60s and low 70s and lows in the 40s or 50s.",
